# CMake build artifacts.
#
# EVERY PATTERN HERE IS ANCHORED ON PURPOSE (#377). A bare `build/` has no
# leading slash, so git matches it at EVERY depth -- a first-party directory
# that happens to be named `build` becomes silently unaddable. #359's
# reorganisation created `scripts/build/` -- PATHREF-OK: #359 renamed it.
# Its six files were tracked only because `git mv` moves already-tracked
# files; a seventh, newly created, would never have been added, and
# `git add` would have reported nothing wrong.
#
# So each pattern below is rooted at a directory where a build tree is actually
# produced. A `scripts/build/` -- PATHREF-OK: #359 renamed it -- or a
# `libs/ra8_core/build/` outside these roots is ordinary tracked source.
#
# Note the deliberate absence of a `build*/` glob: it would match `builders/`,
# which is the collision that made this worth fixing rather than renaming
# around. The separator is always required.
#
# scripts/checks/lint_targets.py:is_build_output() is the matching definition
# for the checkers -- one rule, two readers -- and check_gitignore_scope.py
# fails on any new unanchored directory pattern, so the two cannot drift apart
# again. CMakeFiles/ stays unanchored deliberately: CMake reserves the name and
# nobody can author a source directory called that (the checker's
# RESERVED_DIR_NAMES records that judgement).
/build/
# The mcdc gate's transcript. It is written under build/ now, so this line
# is a second line of defence rather than the fix: a stale root-level copy
# from an older tree once rode into a commit and failed the lint-coverage
# gate, and an ignore rule stops any other producer repeating that.
/mcdc-output.log
/build-*/
/build_*/
/cmake-build-*/
/docs/build/
/examples/**/build/
/examples/**/build-*/
/local-poc/**/build/
/local-poc/**/build-*/
/port/**/build/
/src/**/build/
/src/**/build-*/
/tools/**/build/
CMakeFiles/
CMakeCache.txt
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json

# Downloaded media (comics/manga/manhwa fetched by tools/media_dl). This is
# third-party copyrighted content pulled for LOCAL testing only -- never commit
# or publish it. Applies to the default `downloads/` root anywhere in the
# tree, which is the one pattern here that genuinely cannot be anchored:
# tools/media_dl writes `downloads/` relative to whatever directory it is run
# from, so there is no single root to anchor it to.
# gitignore-scope-ok: media_dl writes it relative to its own cwd
downloads/

# Real-world EPUB test fixtures (copyrighted books used for local pipeline
# testing only -- never committed/published; see tests/fixtures/epub/README.md)
tests/fixtures/epub/real/*.epub

# Compiled firmware artifacts
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
*.lst
*.su

# Compiler intermediates (object files, archives)
*.o
*.obj
*.a
*.lo
*.la

# OS-level crash dumps (e.g. host-side test executables that segfault
# in the Docker test container land at the repo root). Anchored to the
# repo root so they don't shadow legitimate `core/` directories inside
# vendored trees (libs/third_party/tf-psa-crypto/core, etc.).
/core
/core.*
/vgcore.*

# Test build artifacts (build-cov, build-fuzz, build-iwyu, build-scan,
# build-ubsan). Anchored, and hyphen-separated so `tests/builders/` is safe.
/tests/build/
/tests/build-*/
/tests/Unity/

# GCC coverage instrumentation
*.gcov
*.gcda
*.gcno
*.gcov.json.gz

# Coverage report outputs (already covered by build/ above; listed
# explicitly so the directory is greppable)
/build/host-cov/
/build/coverage-html/

# GCC RTL dump files
*.expand

# Doxygen generated output (build/ is already ignored above; listed
# explicitly here so a future change to the build-tree policy still
# keeps the generated HTML out of git). docs/doxygen/ was the output
# directory of the retired Doxyfile.main; kept ignored so stale local
# builds never get committed.
/build/docs/
/build/docs-gate/
/docs/doxygen/
doxygen.log
# Generated Doxygen navigation trees (scripts/gen/gen_doxygen_nav.py, run by
# build_docs.sh). Regenerated on every `make docs`, so kept out of git.
docs/generated/

# Per-page PDF splits of the reference manuals (local browsing aid;
# derived from the committed parent PDFs, 2+ GB if expanded).
docs/reference/ra8d2-datasheet/
docs/reference/ra8d2-hardware-user-manual/
docs/reference/ra8d2-high-temperature-operation/
docs/reference/ra8d2-technical-brief/

# Renesas / vendor IDE artifacts (NOT used here, guarded in case they show
# up). Anchored to the repo root for the same reason as the build trees above:
# `output/` and `ra/` are both plausible source directory names.
#
# `ra/` had already drawn blood in exactly the way #377 describes -- unanchored,
# it swallowed the vendored FSP blob trees, which is the only reason the two
# negations that used to sit below it existed. Anchoring the pattern makes them
# dead code, so they went with it.
.metadata/
.settings/
/HardwareDebug/
/output/
.project
.cproject
*.launch
ra8_cfg.txt
/ra8_gen/
/ra/
/ra8_cfg/

# ARM / Keil / IAR artifacts
*.uvprojx
*.uvoptx
*.ewp
*.eww
*.ewd
/Debug/
/Release/
/Objects/
/Listings/

# SEGGER
*.jdebug
*.jlink

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
*.bak
*.tmp
.DS_Store

# Python / tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
venv/

# Local environment
.env
.env.local
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
doxy_run.txt
.pi-connection
*.dump

# board_sim profiler output (make profile-<app>)
*.speedscope.json
board_sim_profile.*

# Generated e-book artifacts -- build output, regenerated by `make books` from
# the content/library/*.epub sources (the Git-LFS source of truth).
content/compiled/*.rabook
libs/ra8_book/inc/ra8_book_library.h
# NOTE: examples/.../ereader_shelf/library.h is deliberately TRACKED (a
# committed @generated fixture, like the epub/rabook parity fixtures): its
# cover-thumbnail bytes are architecture-dependent to regenerate (libjpeg
# SIMD decode rounding differs x86 vs arm64), so the SIL fb-hash golden pins
# the committed bytes. Regenerate only deliberately (scripts/builders/books.sh)
# and re-pin the golden in the same change.
# Host SD-card images built by tools/mkbookimg (test fixtures).
*.img

# tools/reader_vmem host build artifacts (binary + dSYM + generated #147 traces)
tools/reader_vmem/reader_vmem
tools/reader_vmem/*.trace
tools/reader_vmem/*.dSYM/

# tools/glyph_bench host build artifacts (binary + dSYM)
tools/glyph_bench/glyph_bench
tools/glyph_bench/*.dSYM/

# tools/cache_bench host build artifacts (binary + dSYM) -- were mistakenly tracked
tools/cache_bench/cache_bench
tools/cache_bench/*.dSYM/

# Root-of-trust signing keys must never be committed (see scripts/secrets/rot_provision.sh).
*rot-signing-key*.pem

# ESP32-C6 co-processor firmware: the esp-hosted-mcu SOUP clone that
# coprocessor/esp32c6/build.sh fetches at the pinned commit, plus everything it
# builds underneath (slave/build, dependencies.lock, managed_components,
# generated sdkconfig). None of it is first-party source. Anchored to the
# repo root so it cannot match a directory of that name elsewhere (#377).
/coprocessor/esp32c6/esp-hosted-mcu/
# libFuzzer seed corpus: regenerated deterministically by
# scripts/checks/init_fuzz_corpora.sh (invoked from `make fuzz`), so the seeds
# are a build product, not source. Committing them only lets them drift from
# the generator. Crash reproducers the fuzzer discovers are NOT regenerable,
# so those are carved back in below and must be committed by hand.
#
# NOTE: the corpus contents (not the directory) are ignored, and the
# subdirectories are re-included, so the crash-/leak-/timeout- negations below
# actually take effect. Git cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is
# itself excluded, so `tests/fuzz/corpus/` (directory form) would silently
# defeat the negations.
tests/fuzz/corpus/**
!tests/fuzz/corpus/**/
!tests/fuzz/corpus/**/crash-*
!tests/fuzz/corpus/**/leak-*
!tests/fuzz/corpus/**/timeout-*
